data: {"type": "answer", "text": "Here are a few recommended films similar to ***Parasite* (2019)**\u2014focusing on sharp social commentary, class tension, dark humor, and unpredictable psychological thriller elements\u2014that are **not** in your watch history:\n\n---\n\n### **1. *Burning* (2018)**\n* **Director:** Lee Chang-dong  \n* **Cast:** Yoo Ah-in, Steven Yeun, Jeon Jong-seo  \n* **Why it fits:** Like *Parasite*, this acclaimed South Korean psychological thriller tackles wealth disparity, youth alienation, and class envy in modern South Korea. When an impoverished deliveryman is introduced to a enigmatic, wealthy young man (Steven Yeun) with a bizarre secret hobby, a quiet and deeply unsettling tension begins to build.\n\n---\n\n### **2. *The Handmaiden* (2016)**\n* **Director:** Park Chan-wook  \n* **Cast:** Kim Min-hee, Kim Tae-ri, Ha Jung-woo  \n* **Why it fits:** If you enjoyed the elaborate con, class deception, and jaw-dropping plot twists of *Parasite*, this South Korean thriller is a masterclass in deception. Set in 1930s Korea, a pickpocket is hired as a handmaiden to a wealthy heiress as part of a elaborate plot to steal her fortune\u2014only for dynamic power shifts and double-crosses to upend everything.\n\n---\n\n### **3. *A Normal Family* (2024)**\n* **Director:** Hur Jin-ho  \n* **Cast:** Sol Kyung-gu, Jang Dong-gun, Kim Hee-ae  \n* **Why it fits:** A tense South Korean moral thriller centered around privilege, ethics, and family secrecy. Two brothers\u2014a wealthy defense attorney and an upright pediatrician\u2014meet regularly with their wives for fine dining, but their high-society lives fracture when a disturbing crime involving their teenage children tests their morals and unravels their polished facades.\n\n---\n\n### **4. *I Care a Lot* (2021)**\n* **Director:** J Blakeson  \n* **Cast:** Rosamund Pike, Peter Dinklage, Eiza Gonz\u00e1lez  \n* **Why it fits:** For a sleek, darkly comedic thriller driven by predatory ambition and dynamic class/system exploitation, this film follows a ruthless court-appointed guardian who cons wealthy elderly clients out of their estates\u2014until she accidentally targets someone tied to a dangerous underworld figure.", "iteration": 4, "films": [{"tmdb_id": 496243, "title": "Parasite", "year": 2019, "watched": true, "my_rating": 5.0, "vote_average": 8.49, "poster_url": "https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w342/7IiTTgloJzvGI1TAYymCfbfl3vT.jpg", "overview": "All unemployed, Ki-taek's family takes peculiar interest in the wealthy and glamorous Parks for their livelihood until they get entangled in an unexpected incident."}, {"tmdb_id": 491584, "title": "Burning", "year": 2018, "watched": false, "my_rating": null, "vote_average": null, "poster_url": "https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w342/kXiF80o74fE9gf3Utf9moAI7ar0.jpg", "overview": "Deliveryman Jong-su is out on a job when he runs into Hae-mi, a girl who once lived in his neighborhood. She asks if he'd mind looking after her cat while she's away on a trip to Africa. On her return, she introduces to Jong-su an enigmatic young man named Ben, who she met during her trip. One day Ben tells Jong-su about his most unusual hobby."}, {"tmdb_id": 290098, "title": "The Handmaiden", "year": 2016, "watched": false, "my_rating": null, "vote_average": null, "poster_url": "https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w342/dLlH4aNHdnmf62umnInL8xPlPzw.jpg", "overview": "1930s Korea, in the period of Japanese occupation, a new girl, Sook-hee, is hired as a handmaiden to a Japanese heiress, Hideko, who lives a secluded life on a large countryside estate with her domineering Uncle Kouzuki. But the maid has a secret. She is a pickpocket recruited by a swindler posing as a Japanese Count to help him seduce the Lady to steal her fortune."}, {"tmdb_id": 973628, "title": "A Normal Family", "year": 2024, "watched": false, "my_rating": null, "vote_average": 6.947, "poster_url": "https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w342/pG49LvH6pcfw6oyhYX5iFEtaHS7.jpg", "overview": "Jae-wan, a successful lawyer, takes on the case of a rich executive's son, who has purposely run over and killed a man and left his daughter seriously injured. It's Jae-wan's job to defend a murderer, just another rung on his career's golden-stepped ladder. His younger brother, on the contrary, is a scrupulous and upstanding paediatrician, who always puts the health of his patients over profit and money, often contravening the rules of the private clinic where he works. The brothers meet once a month with their wives for fine dining in expensive restaurants, but when an unexpected situation involving their teenage kids arises, their consciences are questioned and their usual dinner conversation takes an unexpected turn."}, {"tmdb_id": 601666, "title": "I Care a Lot", "year": 2021, "watched": false, "my_rating": null, "vote_average": 6.57, "poster_url": "https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w342/gKnhEsjNefpKnUdAkn7INzIFLSu.jpg", "overview": "A court-appointed legal guardian defrauds her older clients and traps them under her care. But her latest mark comes with some unexpected baggage."}]}

